(491, 'ECE_BH_23_GSLab', 'ECE_BH_23_GSLab', 'Develop a better understanding of important issues related to gender in contemporary India.', 'Analyze basic dimensions of the biological, sociological, psychological and legal aspects of gender', 'Develop a sense of appreciation of women in all walks of life and will be equipped to work and live together as equals.', 'Examine the new laws for women protection & relief, and empower students to understand and respond to gender violence', '', '', 'tb', 'rb'),
(492, 'ECE_BH_23_MC', 'ECE_BH_23_MC', 'Differentiate architectural features and modes of operation of 8086 microprocessor and 8051 microcontrollers.', 'Summarize the addressing modes, instruction set and assembler directives of 8086 Microprocessor and 8051 Micro controller.', 'Write assembly language programs for 8086 Microprocessor and 8051 Microcontroller.', 'Explore serial communication standards and interface various peripheral devices, memory with 8051 microcontrollers.', 'Analyze the architectural features and instruction set of ARM processor', 'Describe the architectural feature of CORTEX and OMAP processors', 'tb', 'rb'),
(493, 'ECE_BH_23_IoAP', 'ECE_BH_23_IoAP', 'Understand the fundamental antenna parameters involved in designing antennas.', 'Examine the radiation pattern of linear wire antennas.', 'Analyze the geometric characteristics of different antenna types.', 'Create varied antenna arrays to optimize gain in the desired direction.', 'Evaluate antenna performance by measuring antenna parameters.', 'Investigate the attributes of wave propagation in diverse atmospheric layers.', 'tb', 'rb'),
(494, 'ECE_BH_23_CS', 'ECE_BH_23_CS', 'Evaluate the types of control systems for real time applications.', 'Compute transfer function of a system by different techniques.', 'Evaluate the time response of systems for standard input signals.', 'Probe the stability of a system using time and frequency domain approach', 'Examine the performance of systems with compensators and controllers', 'Construct state models for continuous & discrete time systems and Comment on controllability and observability of the system', 'tb', 'rb'),
(495, 'ECE_BH_23_BEFA', 'ECE_BH_23_BEFA', 'Understand the Economic Concepts in business decision making process.', 'Familiarize with the cost concepts, market structures.', 'Make use of break-even analysis, CVP Analysis, pricing strategies.', 'Examine financial accounting and analyze various financial statements.', 'Interpret various financial statements by applying different types of ratios.', 'Examine the usefulness of Investment decisions of a company.', 'tb', 'rb'),
(496, 'ECE_BH_23_COOS', 'ECE_BH_23_COOS', 'Visualize the organization of different blocks in a computer. ', 'Utilize the micro-level operations to control different units in a computer.', 'Implement Operating systems in a computer.', 'able to visualize input output organization', 'able to use the memory management', 'able to use file system', 'tb', 'rb'),
(497, 'ECE_BH_23_MCLab', 'ECE_BH_23_MCLab', 'Develop 8086 assembly language programs using macro assembler.', 'Build 8051 assembly language programs for simple arithmetic and logical operations and verify using Keil IDE.', 'Write assembly language programs to configure various peripheral devices using 8051 kits.', 'Interface various input/output devices to ARM Cortex M3 processor using development board and GNU toolchain.', '', '', 'tb', 'rb'),
(498, 'ECE_BH_23_IoAPLab', 'ECE_BH_23_IoAPLab', 'Analyze the radiation patterns of different antennas.', 'Generate different types of signals.', 'Analyze different digital modulation and demodulation schemes', 'Examine various coding techniques.', 'Analyze the radiation patterns of different antennas.', 'Generate different types of signals.', 'tb', 'rb'),
(499, 'ECE_BH_23_AECSLab', 'ECE_BH_23_AECSLab', 'Build sound vocabulary and its proper use contextually', 'Analyze the given text and respond appropriately and develop efficacious writing skills', 'Develop effective speaking skills and Maximize job prospects', 'Plan and make different forms of presentation using various techniques', '', '', 'tb', 'rb'),
(500, 'ECE_BH_23_IPR', 'ECE_BH_23_IPR', 'Understand the fundamental aspects of Intellectual property Rights who are going to play a major role in development and management of innovative projects in industries.', 'Examine Trademarks, Acquisition of Trade Mark Rights and its registration processes.', 'Evaluate various aspects relating to copyrights and its procedure for registration processes.', 'Evaluate with the Trade Secret Law, protection for submission, Unfair Competition.', 'Evaluate on the International Developments in Intellectual Property Rights.', 'Interpret about current trends in IPR and the steps taken by the Government of India in fostering IPR.', 'tb', 'rb'),
(501, 'R18_SL_CSE', 'R18_SL_CSE', 'Make use of resources to gain some fluency programming in Ruby, Perl, TCL and TK', 'Analyze the features of Ruby by embedding in different ways', 'implement by their own confidently.', 'Explain syntax,  variables and various features of  TCL ', 'Elaborate strengths and weakness TCL and select an appropriate language for solving a given problem', 'Examine the TK by embedding in different ways ', 'TB', 'RB'),
(502, 'R18_SL_LAB_CSE', 'R18_SL_LAB_CSE', 'Design and test programs to solve mathematical problems', 'Develop programs Using Ruby Script', 'Develop Programs Using TCL  Script', 'Develop Programs Using  Perl Script', '', '', 'TB', 'RB'),
(503, 'R18_ML_LAB_CSE', 'R18_ML_LAB_CSE', 'Compare Machine Learning algorithms based on their advantages and limitations and use the best one according to situation ', 'Interpret and understand modern notions in data analysis-oriented computing', 'Apply common Machine Learning algorithms in practice and', 'Experiment with real-world data using Machine Learning algorithms.', '', '', 'TB', 'RB'),
(504, 'R18_CD_LAB_CSE', 'R18_CD_LAB_CSE', 'Identify the practical approach of how a compiler works', 'Construct top down and bottom up parsetools', 'Construct LEX and YACC programs', 'Develop new computer languages', '', '', 'TB', 'RB'),
(505, 'R18_NLP_CSE_PE', 'R18_NLP_CSE_PE', 'Show sensitivity to linguistic phenomena and an ability to model them with formal grammars', 'Understand and carry out proper experimental methodology for training and evaluating empirical NLP systems', 'Able to manipulate probabilities, construct statistical models over strings and trees, and estimate parameters using supervised and unsupervised training methods', 'Able to design, implement, and analyze NLP algorithms', 'Able to design different language Modeling Techniques', 'Able to design Applications of Natural Language Processing', 'TB', 'RB'),
(506, 'R18_IRS_CSE_PE', 'R18_IRS_CSE_PE', 'Implementation of Information Retrieval system capabilities and Digital Libraries', 'Implement the Indexing and the Data Structures ', 'Compute the Automatic indexing, Document and term clustering', 'Apply user search techniques to improve the information visualization', 'Implementation of Text Search Algorithms', 'Build the working model for multimedia information retrieval system', 'TB', 'RB'),
(507, 'R18_JP_CSE', 'R18_JP_CSE', 'Illustrate Object Oriented concepts and basics of java programming', 'Make use of the concepts of packages and Interfaces', 'Implement the concepts of multithreading and /or handle run time errors for Java applications', 'Utilize collection framework and /or filemanagement  in Java applications', 'Design real time applications using event handling concepts', 'Develop real time GUI applications using applet, AWT, JDBC and swings', 'TB', 'RB'),
(508, 'R18_BEFA_CSE', 'R18_BEFA_CSE', 'Understand the Economic Concepts in business decision making process', 'Familiarize with the cost concepts, market structures', 'Make use of   breakeven analysis, CVP Analysis, pricing strategies.', 'Examine financial accounting and analyze various financial statements.   ', 'Interpret various financial statements by applying different types of ratios', 'Examine the usefulness of funds flow statement and cash flow statement for better managerial decisions', 'TB', 'RB'),
(509, 'R18_OOPS_CSE', 'R18_OOPS_CSE', 'Make use of object oriented paradigm with concepts of classes and objects', 'Design and Implement programs using C++', 'Apply concepts of Inheritance in real time problems', 'Design solutions for real time problems using Polymorphism and Abstract classes', 'Apply features of stream I/O,  various file handling techniques in C++', 'Analyze the concept  Exception handling using C++ ', 'TB', 'RB'),
(510, 'R18_ITWS_LAB_CSE', 'R18_ITWS_LAB_CSE', 'Construct a Personal Computer and prepare the computer ready to use', 'Prepare the Documents & slide presentations using Word processors and presentation tools', 'Apply internet concepts to connect two or more computers for information sharing', 'Build a dual mode operating system PC by installing OS Software', '', '', 'TB', 'RB'),
(511, 'R18_OOPS_LAB_CSE', 'R18_OOPS_LAB_CSE', 'Apply Object oriented features and C++ concepts', 'Apply the concept of polymorphism and inheritance', 'Implement exception handling and templates', 'Develop applications using Console I/O and File I/O', '', '', 'TB', 'RB'),
(512, 'R18_ADE_LAB_CSE', 'R18_ADE_LAB_CSE', 'Analyze the characteristics of Full wave rectifier', 'Analyze the characteristics of different Transistor amplifier configurations.', 'Implement Boolean expressions using universal logic gates', 'Design and verify simple combinational and sequential circuits using IC s of different logic families.', '', '', 'TB', 'RB'),
(513, 'R22-DE', 'R22-DE', 'Apply the concepts of number systems, and codes in digital system design.', 'Minimize Boolean expression using various techniques.', 'Design combinational logic circuits for given specifications.', 'Design Shift Registers and Counters using flip-flops.', 'Implement logic functions using PLDs and Illustrate the functionality of\nvarious memories.', 'Design and optimize asynchronous sequential circuits.', '1. M. Morris Mano, Digital Design, Third Edition, Pearson Education/PHI.\n2. Albert Paul Malvino and Donald P. Leach, Digital Principles and Applications, 2011, TATA McGraw Hill.\n3. Roth, Fundamentals of Logic Design, 5th Edition, Thomson.', 'RB'),
(514, 'R22-DS', 'R22-DS', 'Implement various operations on linear data structures to solve real world problems.', 'Design solutions using Dictionaries, Hash Tables and time complexity.', 'Implement various kinds of trees and its operations.', 'Describe graph representations and implement traversals.', 'Implement various sorting algorithms.', 'Demonstrate the Pattern matching algorithms and Tries.', '', 'RB'),
(515, 'R22-COSM', 'R22-COSM', 'Distinguish between discrete and continuous random variables', 'Analyze and interpret statistical data using appropriate probability distributions', 'Apply sampling distributions in real world problems', 'Estimate the value for a given parameter by choosing appropriate method', 'Apply suitable test to accept or reject a given hypothesis', 'Apply Stochastic process and Markov process to solve various problems', '', 'RB'),
(516, 'R22-COA', 'R22-COA', 'Implement Micro-operations in Design, Organization and Architecture of a\nbasic computer.', 'Design a suitable Control unit for a decided set of Instructions.', 'Design Hardware and Algorithms for manipulation of data, represented in\ndifferent formats.', 'Implement data transfer with appropriate IO Interface and Interrupt\nmechanism.', 'Choose suitable type of Memory for given purpose', 'Perform Parallel Processing using suitable mechanism', '', 'RB'),
(517, 'R22-OOPJava', 'R22-OOPJava', 'Illustrate Object Oriented concepts and basics of java programming.', 'Explore the concepts of Inheritance, packages and Interfaces.', 'Implement the concepts of exception handling and util package.', 'Apply the knowledge of multithreading to solve problems related to IPC.\n', 'Design GUI applications using event handling concepts & AWT.\n', 'Develop look and feel GUI applications using applets and swing.', '', 'RB'),
(518, 'R22-DS LAB', 'R22-DS LAB', 'Implement with various kinds of linked list and their operations.\n', 'Design programs to implement stack and queue ADT.', 'Implement programs for sorting algorithms.', 'Implement trees and graph traversal and pattern matching algorithms.', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(519, 'R22-OOPJ LAB', 'R22-OOPJ LAB', 'Make use of JDK, Eclipse platform for developing java programs using Oops.\n', 'Build programs using abstract classes and multithreading concepts.', 'Develop programs using GUI components and event handling.\n', 'Design look and feel GUI using swing and applets.', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(520, 'R22-DV LAB', 'R22-DV LAB', 'Understand Tableau fundamentals.', 'Implement visualizations and layouts', 'Explain real world problems by creating GUI using Frames and panels.', 'Create custom charts', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(521, 'R22-GS LAB', 'R22-GS LAB', 'Students will have developed a better understanding of important issues related to\ngender in contemporary India.', 'Students will be sensitized to basic dimensions of the biological, sociological,\npsychological and legal aspects of gender. This will be achieved through discussion\nof materials derived from research, facts, everyday life, literature and film.', 'Students will attain a finer grasp of how gender discrimination works in our society\nand how to counter it.', 'Students will acquire insight into the gendered division of labour and its relation to\npolitics and economics.', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(522, 'R22-DM', 'R22-DM', 'Apply mathematical logic to prove reason and infer the statements.', 'Model the mathematical problems using sets, functions and relations', 'Demonstrate the usage of groups and subgroups. ', 'Apply combinations and permutations to the relevant problems.', 'Make use of Binomial and Multinomial theorems appropriately.', 'Construct the graphs and trees to model the real-world problems', '', 'RB'),
(523, 'R22-BEFA', 'R22-BEFA', 'Understand the Economic Concepts in business decision making process.', 'Familiarize with the cost concepts, market structures.', 'Make use of break-even analysis, CVP Analysis, pricing strategies.', 'Examine financial accounting and analyze various financial statements.', 'Interpret various financial statements by applying different types of ratios.', 'Examine the usefulness of Investment decisions of a company.', '', 'RB'),
(524, 'R22-OS', 'R22-OS', 'Analyze the functionalities and structure of a generic Operating System.\n', 'Evaluate various CPU scheduling algorithms.', 'Analyze process synchronization and IPC mechanisms.  \n', 'Assess the techniques of deadlock avoidance and prevention.', 'Examine different Memory management techniques.', 'Explore file system interface and its operations.', '', 'RB'),
(525, 'R22-DBMS', 'R22-DBMS', 'Identify and classify the components of Database system\n', 'Model the data using ER model and convert into Relational Model.', 'Access and manipulate the data in the databases.', 'Refine the database schema to improve data consistency.', 'Ensure the properties of transactions on Databases.', 'Examine different file organizations and indexing methods.', '', 'RB'),
(526, 'R22-SE', 'R22-SE', 'Ability to translate end-user requirements into system and software requirements, using e.g.\nUML, and structure the requirements in a Software Requirements Document (SRD).\n', 'Identify and apply appropriate software architectures and patterns to carry out high level design of a system and be able to critically compare alternative choices.\n', 'Identify and apply appropriate software architectures and patterns to carry out high level design of a system and be able to critically compare alternative choices.\n', 'Will have experience and/or awareness of testing problems and will be able to develop a simple testing report', 'Analysis the risk factors and create the risk rectification plans to improve the quality.', 'Identify the factors to improve quality based on all concepts and apply in real time case study.', '', 'RB'),
(527, 'R22-OS LAB', 'R22-OS LAB', 'Evaluate CPU Scheduling Algorithms and Memory management techniques.', 'Construct deadlock detection and avoidance algorithms.', 'Solve classical problems of synchronization using semaphores.', 'Evaluate inter process communication mechanisms using system calls and pipes.', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(528, 'R22-DBMS LAB', 'R22-DBMS LAB', 'Design conceptual model (E-R model) for the given database.', 'Formulate the queries using DML, DDL, DCL commands.', 'Enforce integrity constraints on databases.', 'Implement triggers, stored procedures and cursors.', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(529, 'R22-RRP/SRP', 'R22-RRP/SRP', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'RB'),
(530, 'R22-NodeJS Lab', 'R22-NodeJS Lab', 'Build a custom website with HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap and little JavaScript.', 'Demonstrate Advanced features of JavaScript and learn about JDBC.', 'Develop Server – side implementation using Java technologies', 'Develop the server – side implementation using Node JS and Single Page Application using React.', '', '', '', 'RB');
